## Customize flags given to the VM: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars, do not set them here

## Serving directly, every user's keep-alive connection is a BEAM port, and the default limit of 65,536 would cap
## the number of users.
+Q 1000000

## Process heaps and binaries on the "good fit" allocation strategy instead of the default address-order first fit
## (aoffcbf), which also turns off carrier migration between schedulers. A perf profile put a tenth of the CPU in the
## allocators; at real pacing (37,000 and 39,000 users, interleaved) gf took app CPU per request down ~3% in both
## batches, and peak memory 2,474 -> 2,237 MB.
+MHas gf
+MBas gf
